    <h1>Design Systems Engineering</h1>
    <p class="project-subtitle" style="text-align: center; color: var(--color-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem;">Designing experiences that scale</p>

    <p class="project-intro">I approach design systems not just as a collection of visual components, but as a scalable product and a shared language between design and technology. Combining an engineering foundation with advanced UX frameworks, I specialize in architecting, scaling, and maintaining multi-platform design tokens and flexible component libraries. My goal is to reduce design debt, eliminate engineering silos, and streamline enterprise software utilization to drive measurable operational efficiency.</p>

    <h2>Case Study: Multi-Platform System — Point of Sale</h2>
      <p><em>Done in collaboration with Jason Chang, Emery Grearson, James Cradit & Teja Telikicherla.</em></p>

      <h3>The Challenge</h3>
      <p>Managing fragmented interfaces across entirely different user bases—internal corporate colleagues versus everyday consumers—leading to visual inconsistencies and redundant engineering work.</p>

      <h3>The Strategy</h3>
      <p>Co-architected and maintained a comprehensive design system and component library for Point of Sale (POS) infrastructure spanning two distinct platforms:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Colleague-Facing System</li>
        <li>Customer-Facing System</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>The Impact</h3>
      <p>Created a unified foundational language that supported both platforms while allowing for unique, user-specific interaction patterns.</p>

